From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Legowski <jakub.legowski@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 12:20:04 +0200
Subject: fixup! drm/xe/eudebug/xe3p: Per context debugging
 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When running multi-threaded workloads, many threads can hit attentions
simultaneously, causing the GuC to flood the notify queue with repeated
entries for the same exec queue. If the debugger cannot consume events
fast enough, the queue overflows and notifications are lost.

Mitigate this by collapsing consecutive duplicate guc_id entries on
dequeue. Extract tail advancement into notify_queue_advance_tail()
helper and skip over adjacent duplicates before returning. This
reduces queue pressure without changing semantics — the caller still
receives the guc_id and handles all pending attentions for that exec
queue.

Suggested-by: Maciej Patelczyk <maciej.patelczyk@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Jakub Legowski <jakub.legowski@intel.com>
(backported from commit 060412dcdcb1f6ee0dd1d0de827f64d562eb5493 drm-tip-eudebug)
Signed-off-by: Pravalika Gurram <pravalika.gurram@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_gt_debug.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_gt_debug.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_gt_debug.c
index fef1b3b5b..d85717f51 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_gt_debug.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_gt_debug.c
@@ -281,6 +281,15 @@ g2h_exec_queue_lookup(struct xe_guc *guc, u32 guc_id)
 }
 
 #define NOTIFY_MSG_LEN_DW	1
+
+static void notify_queue_advance_tail(struct notify_queue *notify_queue)
+{
+	lockdep_assert_held(&notify_queue->lock);
+
+	notify_queue->tail = (notify_queue->tail + NOTIFY_MSG_LEN_DW) %
+		EUDEBUG_QUEUE_NUM_DW;
+}
+
 static bool get_debug_notify(struct notify_queue *notify_queue, u32 *guc_id)
 {
 	bool ret = false;
@@ -288,8 +297,12 @@ static bool get_debug_notify(struct notify_queue *notify_queue, u32 *guc_id)
 	spin_lock_irq(&notify_queue->lock);
 	if (notify_queue->tail != notify_queue->head) {
 		*guc_id = notify_queue->data[notify_queue->tail];
-		notify_queue->tail = (notify_queue->tail + NOTIFY_MSG_LEN_DW) %
-			EUDEBUG_QUEUE_NUM_DW;
+		notify_queue_advance_tail(notify_queue);
+
+		while (notify_queue->tail != notify_queue->head &&
+		       notify_queue->data[notify_queue->tail] == *guc_id)
+			notify_queue_advance_tail(notify_queue);
+
 		ret = true;
 	}
 	spin_unlock_irq(&notify_queue->lock);
-- 
